must, if required, have a visa in accordance with Regulation (EC) No 810/2009
Regulation (EC) No 810/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 13 July 2009 establishing a Community Code on Visas (Visa Code), OJ. L 243 of 15.9.2009, p. 1; last amended by Regulation (EU) 2019/1155, OJ. L 188 of 12.7.2019, p. 25. or a travel authorisation in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2018/1240
Regulation (EU) 2018/1240 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 12 September 2018 establishing a European Travel Information and Authorisation System (ETIAS) and amending Regulations (EU) No 1077/ 2011, (EU) No 515/2014, (EU) 2016/399, (EU) 2016/1624 and (EU) 2017/2226, OJ. L 236 of 19.9.2018, p. 1; last amended by Regulation (EU) 2021/1152, OJ. L 249 of 14.7.2021, p. 15. (ETIAS travel authorisation);

they meet refugee status in accordance with the Agreement of 28 July 1951

 SR 0.142.30
	 on the Legal Status of Refugees;

they are recognised as stateless persons by Switzerland in accordance with the Treaty of 28 September 1954

 SR 0.142.40
	 on the Legal Status of Stateless Persons;

return counselling in accordance with Article 93 paragraph 1 letter a AsylA

 SR 142.31
	;

on the holder becoming subject to a legally enforceable order for expulsion from Switzerland under Article 66a SCC
SR 311.0 or Article 49a MCC
SR 321.0 ;

has been given a long custodial sentence or has been made subject to a criminal measure in terms of Articles 59–61 or 64 of the SCC

 SR 311.0
	;

has attempted to obtain Swiss citizenship unlawfully or his or her Swiss citizenship has been revoked based on a legally binding ruling issued in connection with a declaration of nullity under Article 36 of the Swiss Citizenship Act of 20 June 2014

 SR 141.0
	;

the foreign national has attempted to obtain Swiss citizenship unlawfully or his or her Swiss citizenship has been revoked based on a legally binding ruling issued in connection with a declaration of nullity under Article 36 of the Swiss Citizenship Act of 20 June 2014 

 SR 141.0
	;

the person concerned was previously refused entry in accordance with Article 14 of the Schengen Borders Code

 See footnote to Art. 7 para. 3.
	 (Art. 64c para. 1 let. b);

an order for expulsion from Switzerland in accordance with Article 66a or 66abis SCC
SR 311.0 or Article 49a or 49abis MCC
SR 321.0 where enforcement has been ordered;

less coercive alternative measures cannot be applied effectively (Art. 28 para. 2 of the Regulation [EU] No 604/2013

 See footnote to Art. 64a para. 1.
	).

five weeks during proceedings under Article 5 of Regulation (EC) No 1560/2003

 Commission Regulation (EC) No 1560/2003 of 2 Sept. 2003 laying down detailed rules for the application of Council Regulation (EC) No 343/2003 establishing the criteria and mechanisms for determining the Member State responsible for examining an asylum application lodged in one of the Member States by a third-country national, OJ L 222 of 5.9.2003, p. 3.
	;

in the case of persons accommodated in a federal centre: the canton responsible for enforcing removal under Article 46 paragraph 1bis third sentence AsylA

 SR 142.31
	, and in other cases the canton in which the federal centre is located;

Article 16 paragraph 3 and 17 of Directive 2008/115/EC

 Directive 2008/115/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 16 Dec. 2008 on common standards and procedures in Member States for returning illegally staying third-country nationals, Amended by OJ L 348 of 24.12.2008, p. 98.
	 for removals to a third country;

Article 28 paragraph 4 of Regulation (EU) No 604/2013

 See footnote to Art. 64a para. 1.
	 for Dublin transfers;

has been sentenced to a long-term custodial sentence in Switzerland or abroad or has been made subject to a criminal law measure in terms of Article 59–61 or 64 of the SCC

 SR 311.0
	;

refugees subject to a legally enforceable order for expulsion from Switzerland under Article 66a or 66abis SCC
SR 311.0 or Article 49a or 49abis MCC
SR 321.0 , or a legally enforceable expulsion order under Article 68 of this Act;

a flat-rate payment for every temporarily admitted person in accordance with Articles 88 paragraphs 1 and 2 and 89 AsylA

 SR 142.31
	;

a claim for supplementary benefits in accordance with the SBA

  SR 831.30
	;

by SEM: if this is necessary for the return of a third-country national in an individual case pursuant to Article 65 paragraph 3 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1240

 See footnote to Art. 5 para. 1 let. abis.
	;

health data collected as part of the epidemic risk assessment in accordance with Article 3 paragraph 1 letter 8 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1240

 See footnote to Art. 5 para. 1 let. abis.
	;

SEM: to determine the state responsible for assessing an asylum application under Regulation (EC) No. 604/2013

 See footnote to Art. 64a para. 1.
	 and in the course of assessing an asylum application if Switzerland is responsible for its processing;

in order to check measures banning entry in order to safeguard Switzerland's internal and external security under the Federal Act of 21 March 1997

 SR 120
	 on Measures to Safeguard Internal Security;

the civil register offices and their supervisory authorities: to identify persons in connection with changes in civil status, to prepare for a marriage ceremony or the registration of a same-sex partnership, and to prevent circumvention of the law on foreign nationals in accordance with Article 97a paragraph 1 CC
SR 210 and Article 6 paragraph 2 of the Same-Sex Partnership Act of 18 June 2004
SR 211.231 ;

the part of the electronic file relating to return under Article 4 paragraph 1 letter d of the Federal Act of 20 June 2003

 SR 142.51
	 on the Information System on Matters relating to Foreign Nationals and Asylum;

content.p:
 SEM and the cantonal authorities entrusted with carrying out the return procedure may in providing return assistance delegate specific tasks to the return counselling agencies (Art. 93 para. 1 let. a AsylA

 SR 142.31
	) and international organisations (Art. 93 para. 3 AsylA). They may delegate tasks to other third parties in connection with organising the return under Article 71 letter b of this Act.

item.p:
a state that is not bound by any of the Dublin association agreements

 These agreements are listed in Annex 1 No 2.
	;

third-country nationals if the conditions set out in Article 20 paragraph 1 of Regulations (EU) 2019/817
See footnote to Art. 110 para. 1. and (EU) 2019/818
See footnote to Art. 110 para. 1. are met;

the FOCBS and the cantonal police authorities as part of their control duties at the Schengen external border: if there is a link to a personal EES dossier containing the personal data in accordance with Articles 16–18 of Regulation (EU) 2017/2226

 See footnote to Art. 103b para. 1.
	;

causing fear and alarm among the public (Art. 258 SCC

 SR 311.0
	),

unlawful association (Art. 275ter SCC

 Art. 275ter SCC was repealed on 1 July 2023 (AS 2023 259).
	),

participation or support for a banned organisation (Art. 74 of the Intelligence Service Act of 25 September 2015

 SR 121
	),

the Agreement of 26 October 2004

